 two copies of the same model get different observations, and the policy assigns each input an action. Both instances read from the same policy node, so I'm weighing the payoffs from the pre-observation position, where I'm equally likely to be in either role, starting with the (pass, pass) outcome.\n\nI'm checking the payoffs: mutual passing gives 2 years each, mutual sending gives 4, and the mixed cases average 2.5 for a policy that sends on one input and passes on the other. Averaged over which role I might be in, passing for both comes out best, and the ex-ante view is the consistent one, since the copies would otherwise each send in the other's situation. I'm concluding the answer is pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10187,"completion_tokens":785,"total_tokens":10972,"cost":0.056448,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.056448,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040748,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0157},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":519,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}